from pathlib import Path
import csv,json,html,zipfile
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
rows=list(csv.DictReader((p/'kit/orders.csv').open()))
clean=list(csv.DictReader((p/'kit/cleaned-orders.csv').open()))
css='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#101c24;color:#eef5ed;font:16px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1050px;margin:auto;padding:56px 24px}h1{font-size:clamp(38px,7vw,76px);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-.045em;max-width:850px}h2{font-size:28px;line-height:1.2}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.15em;color:#c8ec8b;text-transform:uppercase}p{max-width:730px;color:#c3d0d3}a{color:#d3f4a6;overflow-wrap:anywhere}button,.button{display:inline-block;border:1px solid #c8ec8b;border-radius:8px;background:#c8ec8b;color:#122119;padding:13px 19px;font:600 15px system-ui;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none}button[aria-pressed=false]{background:transparent;color:#c8ec8b}section{margin-top:38px;padding:26px;border:1px solid #35474f;border-radius:14px;background:#162730}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:15px/1.7 system-ui;color:#dbe5e8}small{color:#a9bfc5}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:16px}.metric{font-size:32px;font-weight:700;color:#d4f3aa}.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:9px 5px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #35474f}.barrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:60px 1fr 65px;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin:12px 0;font-size:13px}.bar{background:#c8ec8b;height:18px;border-radius:3px}.notice{border-left:3px solid #eac184;padding-left:18px}footer{margin-top:48px;color:#a9bfc5}@media(max-width:500px){main{padding:32px 16px}section{padding:20px 16px}td,th{font-size:12px;padding:8px 3px}}'''
head=lambda title,desc:f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{title}</title><meta name="description" content="{desc}"><style>{css}</style>'
dashboard=head('Sample dashboard | Audit before charts','Explore fictional orders before and after reviewing an exact duplicate. All figures are sample data.')+'''<main><div class="eyebrow">With Hammad / Practice dashboard</div><h1>A good chart starts<br>with a checked number.</h1><p>Fictional orders, 1–6 October 2026 · Currency: AED · Each row is one complete order. This is a learning example, not client results.</p><div><button id="source" aria-pressed="true">Source · 7 rows</button> <button id="clean" aria-pressed="false">Clean · 6 rows</button></div><section><div class="grid"><div><small>Total order amount</small><div class="metric" id="total"></div></div><div><small>Rows in this view</small><div class="metric" id="count"></div></div><div><small>Exact duplicate</small><div class="metric">AED 3,000</div></div></div><p id="status" aria-live="polite"></p></section><section><h2>Orders by day</h2><div id="chart"></div><small>Bar lengths and written values show the same daily totals.</small></section><section><h2>Underlying rows</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Order</th><th>Date</th><th>Currency</th><th>Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table></div></section><footer>Sample data only. Repeated order IDs in real data require review; they may represent legitimate line items.</footer></main><script>'''+f'const sourceData={json.dumps(rows)},cleanData={json.dumps(clean)};'+'''const fmt=n=>n.toLocaleString('en-US');function show(clean){const data=clean?cleanData:sourceData;document.getElementById('total').textContent='AED '+fmt(data.reduce((s,r)=>s+Number(r.amount),0));document.getElementById('count').textContent=data.length;document.getElementById('status').textContent=clean?'Reconciled: AED 15,000 − AED 3,000 = AED 12,000. One reviewed exact duplicate removed.':'Unchecked source: O-1003 appears twice with identical fields. Review before using this total.';document.getElementById('rows').innerHTML=data.map(r=>'<tr><td>'+r.order_id+'</td><td>'+r.date+'</td><td>'+r.currency+'</td><td>'+fmt(Number(r.amount))+'</td></tr>').join('');const daily={};data.forEach(r=>daily[r.date]=(daily[r.date]||0)+Number(r.amount));document.getElementById('chart').innerHTML=Object.entries(daily).map(([d,a])=>'<div class="barrow"><span>Oct '+Number(d.slice(-2))+'</span><div><div class="bar" style="width:'+a/6000*100+'%"></div></div><span>'+fmt(a)+' AED</span></div>').join('');document.getElementById('source').setAttribute('aria-pressed',!clean);document.getElementById('clean').setAttribute('aria-pressed',clean)}document.getElementById('source').onclick=()=>show(false);document.getElementById('clean').onclick=()=>show(true);show(false);</script></html>'''
(p/'kit/dashboard.html').write_text(dashboard)
prompt=(p/'audit-prompt.txt').read_text().strip()
(p/'kit/audit-prompt.txt').write_text(prompt+'\n')
(p/'kit/README.md').write_text('''# AI dashboard audit practice kit

Fictional sample, not client results. Each row is a complete order, not a line item. Currency AED; dates 1–6 October 2026. AI presenter in the accompanying reel.

Run `python3 audit.py` from any directory. It accepts no input path and refuses any sample data changes. It preserves orders.csv, writes cleaned-orders.csv and audit.json, and reports 15000 - 3000 = 12000. No dependencies or network access.

Open dashboard.html in a browser. The source/clean toggle uses embedded snapshots of the bundled checked data. This static dashboard does not automatically load modified CSVs.

Run `python3 test_audit.py` for arithmetic, repeated-ID, date, missing-value and currency checks. Repeated IDs in real datasets can be legitimate: never blindly delete them. Review real data with an approved private tool.
''')
page=head('AI dashboard audit: prompt and practice kit','Audit an original seven-row practice CSV before making charts. Download the prompt, Python checker and interactive dashboard to reconcile totals.')+'''<main><div class="eyebrow">With Hammad / CHECK resource · Local review draft</div><h1>Looks right.<br>Check the number.</h1><p>A polished dashboard can hide a bad total. Practice finding one exact duplicate, preserving your source and reconciling the result before you trust the chart.</p><a class="button" download href="ai-dashboard-audit-kit.zip">Download the practice kit ↓</a> <a href="kit/dashboard.html">Explore the dashboard →</a><section><h2>The seven-row trap</h2><div class="grid"><div><small>Original · 7 rows</small><div class="metric">AED 15,000</div></div><div><small>Exact duplicate removed</small><div class="metric">− AED 3,000</div></div><div><small>Checked · 6 rows</small><div class="metric">AED 12,000</div></div></div><p>Order O-1003 appears twice with the same date, currency and amount. CSV row 4 is retained; row 8 is the exact duplicate. In this fictional example, each row is one complete order, so the duplicate is reviewed and removed.</p><p class="notice">Repeated IDs alone do not prove a mistake. Real orders may span multiple line items. Check the meaning of a row before changing anything.</p></section><section><h2>Copy the audit prompt</h2><p>Use the bundled sample first. Keep real customer data private and use an approved tool.</p><button id="copy">Copy prompt</button><span id="copy-status" role="status"></span><pre id="prompt">'''+html.escape(prompt)+'''</pre></section><section><h2>A review you can reproduce</h2><ol><li>Preserve the original CSV. State what one row represents.</li><li>Confirm AED currency and the 1–6 October 2026 date window.</li><li>Flag repeated IDs, compare every field and separate exact duplicates from conflicts.</li><li>Review the exact duplicate, then retain six complete orders.</li><li>Reconcile AED 15,000 − AED 3,000 = AED 12,000 before creating charts.</li></ol><p>The kit includes original and cleaned CSVs, an audit log, a standard-library Python checker, tests and a working offline dashboard. The checker refuses changed sample data; the dashboard uses embedded snapshots.</p><a href="kit/orders.csv" download>Original CSV</a> · <a href="kit/cleaned-orders.csv" download>Cleaned CSV</a> · <a href="kit/audit.json">Audit log</a></section><section><h2>Read the primary references</h2><p><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/filter-for-or-remove-duplicate-values-662c153f-cf21-4d7b-a5af-a9390648eb37">Microsoft: filter for or remove duplicate values</a><br><a href="https://docs.python.org/3/library/csv.html">Python: CSV file reading and writing</a></p></section><footer>Original fictional sample. Not client results or a performance guarantee. AI presenter.<br>Keyword CHECK is planned for the Instagram release. This local review draft is not a live resource or active DM automation.</footer></main><script>document.getElementById('copy').onclick=async()=>{try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById('prompt').textContent);document.getElementById('copy-status').textContent=' Copied';}catch(e){document.getElementById('copy-status').textContent=' Select and copy the prompt below';}};</script></html>'''
(p/'resource.html').write_text(page)
